[{:adr/consequences "{:kawaraban \"stays non-profit/public-good; ads/engagement-optimization remain structurally\\n              unrepresentable inside it\", :cloud-itonami \"gets a legitimate commercial vertical without forking or reimplementing\\n                  kawaraban\", :isco-2642 \"left as an unpublished :spec stub -- deliberately not built as a duplicate\\n              commercial-journalism blueprint since kawaraban already fills that role\\n              non-commercially\", :real-production-gate \"actually flipping KAWARABAN_ALLOW_LIVE_INGEST=1 against real internet\\n                          endpoints, and actually publishing real posts to the live aozora.app\\n                          PDS, are both explicitly OUT OF SCOPE for this ADR -- deferred to a\\n                          separate, explicitly-confirmed step, same precedent as ADR-2607110100's\\n                          adnetwork :real-production-gate\", :no-changes-to [\"kawaraban lex/*.edn\" \"kawaraban cells/*/state_machine.cljc pure logic\" \"kawaraban's G1-G11 charter\"]}", :adr/authoritative_for ["news actor / media actor requested for aozora.app resolves to: advance the existing\n    non-profit kawaraban (etzhayyim) news medium R0->R1, plus a NEW commercial\n    cloud-itonami-isco-3521 media/broadcast blueprint downstream of kawaraban's public output --\n    not two brand-new actors built from scratch" "kawaraban's own charter (G2 no-ads/no-engagement-rank) structurally conflicts with an ISCO\n    business-model blueprint, so commercialization stays outside kawaraban entirely" "live RSS/Atom ingest reuses kawaraban's existing ingest.cljc gates (normalize-record /\n    normalize-batch) unchanged -- no new gate-bypass path. KAWARABAN_ALLOW_LIVE_INGEST default\n    (unset = refused) is unchanged; flipping it for a real deployment is a separate, explicit,\n    out-of-scope operational step" "cloud-itonami never becomes kawaraban's governance authority -- etzhayyim decision-making is\n    etzhayyim-only (root CLAUDE.md); cloud-itonami's role is strictly downstream commercial\n    consumer of kawaraban's already-public output"], :adr/supersedes [], :adr/superseded_by [], :adr/topic "actor-registration", :adr/related ["orgs/etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-kawaraban" "90-docs/adr/2607022200-com-etzhayyim-tashikame-factcheck-aozora-actor-r0.md" "90-docs/adr/2607032300-aozora-per-actor-authority-firehose-appview.md" "90-docs/adr/2607110100-cloud-itonami-adnetwork-advertiser-ops.edn" "orgs/etzhayyim/root/80-data/kotoba-rad/kawaraban.identity.journal.edn" "orgs/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-3521" "orgs/kotoba-lang/occupation/resources/kotoba/occupation/registry.edn" "orgs/kotoba-lang/kotobase-peer/src/kotobase_peer/core.cljc" "orgs/kotoba-lang/kotobase-cljc-worker" "orgs/gftdcojp/app-aozora/40-engine/cljs/pds"], :adr/status "accepted", :adr/id "adr-2607110200-kawaraban-r0-r1-cloud-itonami-isco-3521-media-broadcast", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/last_verified "2026-07-10", :adr/decision "{:split \"two-layer design: kawaraban (etzhayyim, unchanged charter) = the news actor, advanced R0->R1.\\n   cloud-itonami-isco-3521 (new, public, blueprint-only) = the commercial media/broadcast actor,\\n   downstream consumer of kawaraban's public output. kawaraban's lex/*.edn and cell logic are not\\n   touched by this ADR.\", :kawaraban-r0-r1 {:live-fetch {:file \"methods/live_fetch.cljc (new)\", :design \"fetches + parses RSS/Atom, then feeds records through the EXISTING\\n             ingest/normalize-record + normalize-batch -- G1/G3/G4 gates inherited, not\\n             reimplemented. fetch fn is injectable; this session's tests use local fixtures only,\\n             no live internet calls made\", :allowlist \"data/outlets/allowlist.edn (new): state/public-broadcaster + non-profit press only\\n                (NHK World-Japan, BBC News World, Deutsche Welle, France 24, RTHK, CBC News, ABC\\n                News Australia, NPR, PBS NewsHour, AP, Al Jazeera, UN News), each already\\n                :access :open per outlet.edn lexicon\", :gate \"KAWARABAN_ALLOW_LIVE_INGEST semantics and default (unset = refused) unchanged. This ADR\\n           IS the Council-ADR ratification the cells' own solve() comments ask for, but ratifying\\n           != flipping the env var against real internet endpoints in a real deployment -- that\\n           remains a separate, explicit, out-of-scope operational step for the founder/Council\\n           (currently 1/1 = the owner)\"}, :aozora-publish {:files [\"src/kawaraban/cacao.clj (new, port of tashikame.cacao)\" \"src/kawaraban/aozora.clj (new, port of tashikame.aozora, collection\\n             com.etzhayyim.apps.kawaraban per the pre-recorded RAD entry)\" \"src/kawaraban/publisher.cljc (new, port of tashikame.publisher, MockPublisher default)\"], :gating \"publication itself follows ADR-2606281500 (autonomous-by-default, no per-post\\n             Council/operator prior restraint) -- gated only by the existing structural checks\\n             (G1/G3/G4/G7/G9/G11 via route/validate + cell state machines), not by a new approval\\n             step\"}, :maturity-doc \"MATURITY.md updated to record R1: live-fetch code-complete + tested, default off\"}, :cloud-itonami-isco-3521 {:repo \"orgs/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-3521 (new, public, AGPL-3.0-or-later)\", :template \"exact cloud-itonami-isco-* sibling template (README/GOVERNANCE/CONTRIBUTING/\\n              SECURITY/CODE_OF_CONDUCT/LICENSE/docs/business-model.md/docs/operator-guide.md/\\n              docs/samples/operator-console.html/blueprint.edn) -- documentation only, no code,\\n              matching every sibling repo\", :business \"consumes kawaraban's already-public headline+link+excerpt output to produce daily\\n              video/audio news-digest, a syndication API (attribution-required news-ticker\\n              widget), white-label editorial curation -- never touches kawaraban's lexicon/cells,\\n              never reproduces full text, Media Broadcast Governor refuses misattribution/\\n              fabrication\", :governance-boundary \"cloud-itonami is NOT kawaraban's governance authority -- etzhayyim\\n                          decision-making stays etzhayyim-only; cloud-itonami's role is strictly\\n                          the downstream commercial consumer\", :registration \"not west-managed (matches sibling isco-* convention: blueprint repos are\\n                  standalone); no RAD identity (not an actor, a business blueprint)\"}}", :db/id -1, :adr/problem "{:source \"owner request 2026-07-10: collect/organize world news at aozora.app 'as cloud-itonami',\\n           design+integrate a news actor and a media actor\", :investigated [\"kawaraban (orgs/etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-kawaraban) already IS a mature news-medium actor:\\n    mirrors real outlets as headline+link+<=280char excerpt only (never full body), wires\\n    first-party actor events into matching 面 sections, G1-G11 charter gates pinned in lexicon\\n    const/enum, 54 tests green -- but stuck at R0 (offline-only; live RSS/firehose ingest and\\n    aozora publish both explicitly Council-ADR-gated per the cells' own solve() comments)\" \"kawaraban's RAD identity journal (kawaraban.identity.journal.edn) already carries\\n    :rad/aozora-pds 'https://pds.aozora.app' and :rad/aozora-collection\\n    'com.etzhayyim.apps.kawaraban' (tx 4) -- aozora wiring was already intended, just unbuilt\" \"tashikame (orgs/etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-tashikame) is the concrete precedent for publishing to\\n    aozora: com.atproto.server.createSession -> com.atproto.repo.createRecord with a depth-1\\n    self-minted CACAO; the custom com.etzhayyim.* lexicon is only the record collection name\" \"cloud-itonami-isco-* (org cloud-itonami) is a fleet of ~80 documentation-only 'Open Occupation\\n    Blueprint' repos (no code) for forkable commercial businesses; ISCO 2642 Journalists and 3521\\n    Broadcasting and Audiovisual Technicians exist as unpublished :spec stubs in\\n    kotoba-lang/occupation's registry.edn\" \"owner explicitly wants the cloud-itonami side to be commercially viable, but kawaraban's own\\n    G2 gate makes ads/sponsored-placement/engagement-ranking unrepresentable at the lexicon level\\n    -- a straight ISCO business-model wrapper around kawaraban itself would conflict with its own\\n    charter\"], :risk \"building a brand-new isco-2642 Journalists commercial blueprint from scratch would\\n         duplicate kawaraban's already-built, charter-vetted, 54-test-covered pipeline, and would\\n         either fork the charter (weakening G1-G11) or produce a redundant parallel system; folding\\n         kawaraban itself under cloud-itonami would be a cross-org governance category error since\\n         etzhayyim's decision-making is constitutionally etzhayyim-only\"}", :adr/alternatives "[{:option \"build a new cloud-itonami-isco-2642 (Journalists) commercial blueprint from scratch\", :rejected_because \"directly duplicates kawaraban's already-built, charter-vetted pipeline and\\n                      would either weaken kawaraban's own G1-G11 charter or produce a redundant\\n                      parallel news-collection system\"} {:option \"fold kawaraban itself under cloud-itonami / gftdcojp ownership\", :rejected_because \"cross-org governance category error -- etzhayyim's decision-making is\\n                      constitutionally etzhayyim-only (root CLAUDE.md), not transferable to a\\n                      gftdcojp business-OS actor\"} {:option \"leave kawaraban at R0 and only build the cloud-itonami side\", :rejected_because \"isco-* blueprints are documentation-only by convention; without kawaraban's\\n                      R1 advance there is no actual collection pipeline feeding aozora, so the\\n                      'collect and organize world news' request goes unfulfilled\"}]", :adr/authoritative true, :adr/title "ADR-2607110200: kawaraban R0→R1 (live RSS ingest + aozora publish) + cloud-itonami-isco-3521 media/broadcast actor", :adr/addendum "{:date \"2026-07-10\", :trigger \"same-day go-live (owner-approved 'live RSS ingest' + 'real aozora publish', per-actor posting) drove\\n            hundreds of com.atproto.repo.createRecord writes from kawaraban's per-outlet mirror\\n            actors + cloud-itonami's media actor onto the SHARED operator graph\\n            (yoro-social-v2, derived from YORO_OPERATOR_DID+YORO_DB_NAME) in one day, far\\n            outrunning the 5-minute fold cron's steady-state assumption\", :symptom \"pds.aozora.app listRecords/getRecord hung 15-40s+; a direct read against\\n             kotobase.aozora.app's datoms endpoint for the same graph 503'd with Cloudflare\\n             error 1102 (CPU time exceeded) at ~49s -- confirmed CPU-bound decode/merge of a\\n             large unfolded novelty backlog, not just R2 I/O wait\", :fixes {:kotobase-peer \"src/kotobase_peer/core.cljc pmap-async (the novelty tx-block concurrent-fetch\\n                  helper) fired ALL blocks via one unbounded js/Promise.all -- capped to\\n                  24-in-flight batches. A reader-conditional syntax slip while editing\\n                  (#?(:cljs form1 form2) only pairs :cljs with form1; form2 -- the defn itself\\n                  -- silently drops from compilation as an unrecognized feature key) briefly\\n                  regressed pmap-async to undefined, caught by npm run test:cljs (78 tests /\\n                  165 assertions) before deploy\", :kotobase-cljc-worker \"wrangler.jsonc had no explicit limits.cpu_ms (plan default). Batching alone\\n                       didn't fix the 1102 -- the real ceiling was synchronous CPU decode/merge\\n                       time, not concurrency. Raised to 300000 (the documented Workers Standard\\n                       usage-model max)\", :fold-cron \"no code/config change -- app-aozora-pds's existing */5 * * * * Cron Trigger\\n              (FOLD_CRON_ENABLED=1, OPERATOR_SECRET already configured) simply needed the\\n              raised CPU budget to complete a catch-up fold of the backlog into a fresh cold\\n              snapshot on its next scheduled run. No manual secret access or one-off fold\\n              trigger was needed\"}, :verified \"post-fold: direct kotobase.aozora.app graph read 129s (pre-fold, just inside\\n              the raised budget) -> 7.2s; pds.aozora.app listRecords (kawaraban bbc-world\\n              mirror) hanging(15-40s+) -> 4.4s, real article data intact (no data loss)\", :scope \"infrastructure-only -- no change to kawaraban's or cloud-itonami media actor's\\n           lexicon, Media/Charter Governor semantics, or G1-G11 gates\"}"}]